  "design": [
    "One logical source record retains immutable compiler code; each realm has a separate execution instance and caches. Detailed captures expose the actual shared source-record identity.",
    "Opaque owners retain no guest values or strong realm roots. Realm weak associations are pruned before heap slot reuse; escaped functions retain their source records and otherwise unused code is reclaimed after owners drop.",
    "Foreign runtime/reset handles reject using actual atom-sequence ownership, preserving private brands, fresh objects and realm-specific template identity.",
    "All incoming function-constructor and prototype-info assertions remain intact. Named native-info lookup now checks canonical atom identities and keeps the exact prototype transition out of ordinary-key text inspection."
  ],
  "limitations": [
    "All-parallel goal remains open. Latest complete stable321 full1795/5015 and pinned e9 full1821/4727; newer pinned321 audit is running separately.",
    "Functional milestone only: fixed-work8valid0clean. Linux collector records RSS/output but no PMU counters; direct user-only perf_event_open returns ENOENT. Incoming failed1percent instruction guards are retained, not claimed passed or isolated to one change.",
    "The initial new owned-Script tests exposed bypassed program-cache initialization:661existing passed and2new failed. Corrected by the shared complete initializer; unchanged new tests now pass within663/663.",
    "Matched15-case assertion/OS family has no losses or skip changes, with no new full-case gain in this batch.",
    "Native ContextifyScript, VM timeout/cache/code-generation and broader sourceURL/prototype warmup behavior remain incomplete. No placeholder class or false capability was added."
  ],
